What:		/sys/class/power_supply/cps8601-stylus/bt_address
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-pm@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Bluetooth address of the stylus docked on the charger, as the
		stylus sent it over the charging coil and the charger checked
		it, in the colon-separated form, most significant byte first,
		lower case (for example c0:87:06:07:fe:68). Reading fails with
		ENODATA while no identified stylus is docked.

		When an identified stylus docks or leaves, the power supply
		sends a change uevent with these variables:

		ACCESSORY_TYPE=stylus
		ACCESSORY_PRESENT=1 (docked) or 0 (left)
		ACCESSORY_BT_ADDRESS=<the address above>

		Access: Read

What:		/sys/class/power_supply/cps8601-stylus/bt_capacity
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-pm@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		State of charge of the docked stylus as userspace read it over
		Bluetooth. The stylus reports its state of charge over the coil
		only when it stops charging, so the charger relies on this
		value to charge a full stylus again: a write at or below
		charge_control_start_threshold (default 90) restarts charging
		of a stylus that had reported full. The value written is also
		reported as capacity. Writing fails with ENODEV while no
		identified stylus is docked. Reading returns the last state of
		charge, written here or reported over the coil, and fails with
		ENODATA from the time a stylus leaves, or another one is
		identified, until either of them sets it again.

		Access: Read, Write

		Valid values: 0 - 100 (percent)
